Priority: P0
Title:    [P0] Remediate /usr/sbin/php-fpm8.3 (VULNERABLE, SAPI: fpm)
Steps:
  1. Upgrade php8.3-fpm to >= 8.3.35-1+deb12u2 via distro package manager.
  2. Temporary configuration mitigation (applies to CVE-2026-109619 only; not a fix):
     Create drop-in INI file /etc/php/8.3/fpm/conf.d/99-mitigation.ini:
       session.upload_progress.enabled = 0
     Alternatively, in FPM pool config (/etc/php/8.3/fpm/pool.d/www.conf):
       php_admin_value[session.upload_progress.enabled] = 0
Commands:
  [Upgrade Debian/Ubuntu package] apt-get install --only-upgrade php8.3-fpm
Restart Hints:
  - reload php-fpm (e.g. systemctl reload php8.3-fpm)
Notes:    WARNING: A configuration mitigation is a temporary risk reduction only and is NOT a fix. CVE-2026-109618 has no known configuration mitigation; upgrading PHP is required.
